{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"baa925c2686f57392083336656dee348d5ab89a03a0928a9be9e28f7a7a0308f","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM review kernel model configuration","key_entities":["MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS","src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py","model_max_output_tokens","nova-pro","nova-2-lite","nova-lite","nova-micro","DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS","us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0","bedrock:"],"problem_keywords":["model_max_output_tokens","Amazon Nova","Bedrock","output_token_ceiling","validation_exception"],"propositions":["MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS lookup lacks Amazon Nova model entries, causing Bedrock to reject Nova calls with ValidationException when output tokens exceed the 10,000 ceiling.","Nova Pro and Nova Lite family models on Bedrock have a maximum output token limit of 10,000, not the 16,000 fallback default.","Substring matching in model_max_output_tokens requires explicit entries for both nova-lite and nova-2-lite forms to distinguish them, plus full Bedrock inference-profile IDs.","Plan-review LLM phase collapses to INDETERMINATE status for Nova models until the token ceiling table is patched, blocking model comparison experiments."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787542344524249001,"uuid":"51c914a7-7a5a-47b6-bdb8-74f40e1fd5a5"}